./docs/specs/SLACK-ORG-INTEGRATION-SPEC.eli16.md:9:Instar already has a decent Slack adapter (it can read channels, respond when mentioned, handle files). It also already stores a `permissions` list on each user. **But here's the bug we found: nothing ever *checks* that list.** There's literally a `hasPermission()` function in the code that is never called anywhere. Permissions were just shown to the AI as a note and we *hoped* it would behave. That's a wish, not a rule.
